+# Phase 4.1 Plan 01: MuninnDB Integration Summary
+
+**MuninnDB cognitive memory sidecar integrated via async httpx REST client with dual-write capture, parallel pgvector+ACTIVATE search, and dedicated activate tool (13 MCP tools total)**
+
+## Performance
+
+- **Duration:** ~45 min (across 2 sessions with human-verify checkpoint)
+- **Started:** 2026-03-05
+- **Completed:** 2026-03-05
+- **Tasks:** 3 (+ 1 bug fix deviation)
+- **Files created:** 1 (promaia/brain/muninn.py)
+- **Files modified:** 1 (promaia/brain/mcp_server.py)
+
+## Accomplishments
+- MuninnDB REST client wrapper (170 lines) with health, write, write_batch, activate, stats, close methods and async lazy singleton
+- Brain MCP server upgraded from 12 to 13 tools: dual-write in capture, parallel retrieval in search, new activate tool
+- 32 existing brain.memories seeded into MuninnDB zbrain-vault via individual POST calls (batch endpoint workaround)
+- Full graceful degradation verified: MuninnDB down does not affect capture or search
+- Human-verified end-to-end: MuninnDB Web UI shows engrams, capture dual-writes confirmed, search shows both sources
+
+## Task Commits
+
+Each task was committed atomically:
+
+1. **Task 1: Create MuninnDB REST client wrapper** - `180e04e` (feat)
+2. **Task 2: Modify MCP server -- dual-write capture, parallel search, activate tool** - `9071754` (feat)
+3. **Task 2b: [Bug fix] write_batch vault workaround** - `d5ea814` (fix)
+4. **Task 3: Configure MuninnDB, seed memories, verify end-to-end** - checkpoint:human-verify APPROVED (no code changes, setup-only)
+
+## Files Created/Modified
+- `promaia/brain/muninn.py` - Async httpx REST client for MuninnDB with 6 methods (health, write, write_batch, activate, stats, close) and get_muninn() async lazy singleton
+- `promaia/brain/mcp_server.py` - Upgraded from 12 to 13 tools: capture handler adds MuninnDB dual-write, search handler adds parallel MuninnDB ACTIVATE retrieval with source labels, new _handle_activate handler with score component breakdown
+
+## Decisions Made
+- **httpx over SDK:** muninndb Python SDK installs zero code files on Python 3.14 due to packaging bug. Direct REST calls via httpx (already a dependency) are reliable.
+- **Individual writes for batch:** MuninnDB v0.3.6-alpha /api/engrams/batch endpoint ignores the vault field, always writing to default vault. Worked around with sequential individual POST /api/engrams calls that correctly respect the vault parameter.
+- **Best-effort dual-write:** MuninnDB write in capture handler is wrapped in try/except after all Postgres operations complete. Failure logs a warning but never changes the user-facing return value.
+- **One-time health check:** get_muninn() checks MuninnDB health once on first call and caches the result. Prevents repeated connection attempts on every tool call when MuninnDB is down.
+- **Embedder limitation accepted:** MuninnDB Google embedder failed to initialize (text-embedding-004 not available on v1beta API), resulting in semantic_similarity=0 in ACTIVATE responses. This is a MuninnDB server configuration issue, not a code issue. User approved proceeding -- the integration code is correct and will benefit from embeddings once MuninnDB updates their API version.
+
